      "text": "The bug is the call `qc.u1(...)`. `QuantumCircuit.u1` was removed in Qiskit 1.0, so the script fails before transpilation. The equivalent current API is the phase gate `qc.p(...)`, which is the same operation as U1(λ) = diag(1, e^{iλ}). I kept the transpile call and its basis unchanged; the transpiler tracks the global phase when it rewrites the gate.\n\n```python\nfrom qiskit import QuantumCircuit, transpile\n\nlam = 0.5\n\nqc = QuantumCircuit(1)\n# FIX: qc.u1 was removed from QuantumCircuit in Qiskit 1.0 -> use the equivalent phase gate qc.p, because P(lam) is the same operation as U1(lam)\nqc.p(lam, 0)\n\ntranspiled = transpile(qc, basis_gates=['rx', 'ry', 'rz'])\nprint(transpiled)\n```",
      "type": "text"
    }
